    ├── Pitfalls   : PyCrypto's AES.new accepts key/IV as str/bytes interchangeably; cryptography requires bytes and explicit padding 
    │   (e.g., PKCS7) — the current null-byte padding is non-standard and must be replicated manually; cryptography's API is 
    │   lower-level: Cipher(algorithm, mode) + encryptor()/decryptor() instead of a single object with encrypt/decrypt methods; 
    │   pycryptodome is a near drop-in replacement (same import path), but still inherits some PyCrypto quirks; cryptography is 
    │   preferred for new code; Fixed IV (b'0000000000000000') is a security anti-pattern — any migration should ideally switch to 
    │   random IVs prepended to ciphertext
    ├── Constraints: crypto_required, requires_connector
    └── The code uses PyCrypto's AES implementation for CBC-mode encryption with a fixed IV and null-byte padding. Both 'cryptography'
        (via hazmat.primitives.ciphers) and 'pycryptodome' (drop-in replacement for PyCrypto) provide equivalent AES-CBC 
        functionality. PyCrypto is unmaintained and has known HIGH-severity CVEs (GHSA-6528-wvf6-f6qg, GHSA-cq27-v7xp-c356), making 
        migration strongly advisable.

